=== REBUILD NEEDED -- nothing was published. ===

EdSharp_Setup.exe was built from version 5.0.2, not 5.0.3.
Publishing it would tag a release whose program reports the wrong version,
and F11 would misbehave for your users.

The version files are now set to 5.0.3.  Rebuild, then re-run:

  1. BuildEdSharp.cmd
  2. Compile EdSharp_Setup.iss in Inno Setup
  3. git add -A  /  git commit  /  git push
  4. tagRelease                  (publishes 5.0.3; it will NOT bump again)

To avoid this extra cycle, settle the version BEFORE building next time:

  tagRelease -PrepareOnly     bumps only if the current version is already out,
                              writes the .iss, publishes nothing
  BuildEdSharp.cmd  ->  Inno Setup  ->  git add/commit/push  ->  tagRelease

That way the build already carries the version being tagged, and the final
tagRelease simply publishes it.

Committing the version files so they are not lost: EdSharp_Setup.iss
  > git add EdSharp_Setup.iss

  > git commit -m EdSharp 5.0.3
